Experiment 7: Develop a program to read the pH Value of a various substances like milk, lime and water.

AIM: To develop an Arduino-based system to measure and display the pH
value of various substances such as milk, lime, and water using a pH sensor.



COMPONENTS:

Sl. No.	
Quantity	
Component
1	1	Arduino Uno R3
2	1	USB Cable
3	3	Jumper Wire
4	1	pH Sensor



CIRCUIT CONNECTIONS:



Ultrasonic Sensor	Arduino
GND	GND
V+	5V
Po	Ao



SETUP:

1.   Connect the pH sensor to the Arduino Uno as per the circuit connections given.
2.   Connect the Arduino Uno to the computer using the USB cable.
3.   Open the Arduino IDE on your computer.
4.   Go to: Tools → Board → Arduino Uno.
5.   Go to: Tools → Port → and select the COM port assigned to your
Arduino.
6.   Create a new sketch and type the pH measurement program provided.
7.   Click Upload to upload the sketch to the Arduino board.
8.   Open the Serial Monitor and set the baud rate to 9600.
9.   Immerse the pH sensor probe into different substances such as milk,
lime juice, and water one by one.
10. Observe the  pH values displayed on the Serial Monitor.
 

CODE:

#define SensorPin A0 float voltage, phValue;


void setup() { Serial.begin(9600); Serial.println("Calibrating pH Sensor...");
}


void loop() {
int sensorValue = analogRead(SensorPin);
voltage = sensorValue * (5.0 / 1023.0);  // convert to voltage


// Use your calibrated formula phValue = (-7.5 * voltage) + 17.5;


Serial.print("Voltage: "); Serial.print(voltage); Serial.print(" V | pH: "); Serial.println(phValue);

delay(1000);
}


